# ---- ADDENDUM 2026-11-13 · Bassline 2.0 — time, the notes it chooses, phrase; on the compatibility graph (everything above kept verbatim — Axiom 9)
# his words (2026-11-13T12:31:19Z, verbatim): "I love the bassline, needs more depth and control. like tempo and the cord tool. bassline is high
#   leverage." · map: specs/eravos.2026-11-13-session.map.spec · status: SPEC — its UI shown to him before it is built (CLAUDE.md)
# what it has (1.1): rhythm (5) · energy · octave · length · own chords + bars/chord · FEEL slides, ghosts, jumps, move, humanize, accent,
#   follow, seed · 16 step lanes (level, octave, slide) · motion, perform. What it lacks: control of TIME and of WHICH NOTES (Chords has
#   Voicing and Tension; Bassline has root, a fifth by chance, one approach step).
config 2.0 (each default plays 1.1's notes — tested, as 1.1 was against 1.0):
  TIME     rate 1/4 · 1/8 · 1/16 (default) · 1/8T · 1/16T — its step against the transport · feel half · normal (default) · double · swing
           0…1 (0 default; or "follow the Groove's") · phrase 1 · 2 · 4 (default: as now) · 8 bars · answer 0…1 (the second half of a
           phrase answers the first: the same rhythm, its notes moved — 0 default)
  NOTES    pool: root (default) · root + fifth · root + octave · chord tones · scale · approach (chromatic / scale steps into the next chord) ·
           walking (a note each beat, toward the next chord) — the way Chords has Voicing · tension 0…1 (how often it leaves the root for the
           pool's other notes — 0 default; 1.1's move stays as it is) · range low … high (MIDI; default the octave knob's two octaves) ·
           anticipate 0…1 (lands the next chord's root up to an eighth early — 0 default)
  STEPS    the lanes gain pitch (a degree or an interval locked on that step: −, root, 3rd, 5th, 7th, octave, ±1 step) and rest (a step that
           never plays) — the generator fills every step not locked · step count 8 · 16 (default) · 32
  LIVE     every one changes the line while it plays (axiom 4); every number a modulation input (mod.knob.*) as now
on the graph (specs/eravos.compat-graph.spec): Bassline is written with its ports and variables as data from the start (in: chord, step,
  transport, key, modulation · out: note) — the first tool native to the graph; its UI as parts with roles (tempo/rate, key, step grid,
  energy: specs/eravos.ui-field.spec ADDENDUM 2026-11-13) so it merges with Chords and its instrument.
acceptance 2.0: defaults = 1.1's notes (seeded, bar for bar) · rate / feel / swing place notes where they are asked (to the sample) · each pool
  stays in the pool and in the key · range never left · anticipation lands before the bar by ≤ an eighth · a locked step plays its lock, a
  rest never plays · a change while it plays reaches the next step · the tool contract
phases: B2.0 this spec · B2.1 the UI preview shown to him · B2.2 the engine (TIME, NOTES, STEPS) + tests · B2.3 the UI after his yes

# ---- ADDENDUM 2026-11-13 (2) · Bassline 2.0 BUILT (3.186) — shown to him, waiting for his yes (everything above kept verbatim — Axiom 9)
# his words (2026-11-13T15:58:04Z): "Okay. The bassline tool. Way more depth. I like that tool. A lot."
built (engine 2.0.0, tested — bass-gen.test.js, 8 new checks):
  TIME   feel half · normal · double (its own rhythm over two bars, as written, or twice a bar) — the spec's "rate" becomes feel: the rhythms are
         written in 16ths, so half / double move them while keeping them its own · swing 0…1 (the off 16ths late, a triplet's third at 1) ·
         phrase 1 · 2 · 4 · 8 + answer 0…1 (the second half of each phrase: the same rhythm, notes up a third or a fifth, seeded)
  NOTES  pool root · root + fifth · root + octave · chord tones · scale · walking, left by tension 0…1 (never the first of the bar; walking steps
         toward the next chord on the beats) · range (span) 1–3 octaves above Octave, higher notes folded down · ahead (anticipation) 0…1: an
         8th before a bar whose own chord changes, the next chord's root
  STEPS  lock lane (· root 3rd 5th 7th octave +1 −1, in scale steps from the bar's chord) · rest lane (the step never plays)
  not built (left open): a step count of 8 / 32 · triplet rates on the grid (swing gives the triplet feel)
  the window itself is unchanged; TIME, NOTES and the two lanes are on its page's Steps tab (power without overwhelm)
proof: defaults = 1.1's notes bar for bar (and a pool with no tension changes nothing); half = 4, normal = 8, double = 16 notes of 'every beat'
  in two bars; swing puts notes a third of a step late; a fifth-pool stays in key, downbeats unchanged; a lock on step 4 plays the chord's fifth,
  a rest on step 2 never plays; range 1 keeps every note under two octaves; ahead plays the next root on step 14; answer moves only the second half.

